{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "quiet-stretch-depth-telemetry-readonly",
    "parent": "stall-abort-quantile-off-identity-path",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Measure-only: joint distribution of longest quiet stretch vs. final prefix depth, no gate",
    "description": "Add no termination logic at all. In spur-core/src/simulator/util_stats.rs accumulate, per completed run, a 2-D histogram keyed by (bucketed longest no-act stretch, final prefix depth) plus the same histogram split by end_reason (plan_complete vs iterations_exhausted vs deadlock), using the existing per-delivery 'acted' bit already computed for deliveryEffects. Emit as util_stats.quietStretchByDepth. Gate the accumulation behind a config field quiet_stretch_telemetry (default false) and enable it only in a one-off probe config, never in scheduler_configs/loop/general_vr.json, so the default hot path is untouched; keep the counter update out of the per-step path (fold at run end from a single u32 carried in the explorer's run-local state). Success criterion is purely informational: does any quiet-stretch quantile exist above which the conditional probability of ever reaching depth>=6 is near zero? If no such cut exists, the entire early-termination family is closed for good.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "util_stats deliveryEffects acted bit"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 3,
    "expectedCost": 1.5,
    "rationale": "Two stall-abort attempts have now been rejected while guessing at the threshold's population and the signal's meaning. The 14-15% act rate on biased/delayed/restarted deliveries suggests quiescence and depth production are positively, not negatively, associated — but that is inference from marginals. One cheap read-only run settles whether any separating cut exists, and either unlocks a correctly-calibrated third attempt or permanently retires a family that has already cost two full sequential evaluations.",
    "generalityArgument": "It measures only the relationship between 'no delivery changed anything' and achieved interleaving depth, both protocol-agnostic quantities defined by the simulator, and it changes no scheduling decision, so it cannot encode protocol-specific knowledge.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-29T15:05:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "[unparked iteration 5362] Cheap offline sizing for the one endorsed direction (inert-tail reclamation) and picks the cutoff without a 300s campaign; falsifier: if deep prefixes routinely follow long quiet stretches, any tail cutoff is unsafe and candidate 1 withdraws."
  },
